        "problem": "Find $|r(4)|$ given that $r(t)=\u27e8\\frac{10}{t+1},\\,2t-2,\\,t-1\u27e9.$",
        "worked_solution": "Evaluating the function at $t=4,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r(4) & =\u27e8\\frac{10}{4+1},\\,2(4)-2,\\,4-1\u27e9 \\\\  & =\u27e82,\\,6,\\,3\u27e9.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nComputing the magnitude of this vector, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|r(4)| & =\\sqrt{{(2)}^{2}+{(6)}^{2}+(3)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{4+36+9} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{49} \\\\  & =7.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
